Z||000016||mrfixit58||08-01-2001||08:01 AM||||Hey Aus,<P>You say your working on the side scoops. Does that include the piece the is to be mounted on the lower portion of the doors?<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000017||AusFiero||08-01-2001||08:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>Hey Aus,<P>You say your working on the side scoops. Does that include the piece the is to be mounted on the lower portion of the doors?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well kinda Roy. Actually it includes complete lower sections of the door skins so you don't have to mould them in. Trying to make everything really easy to fit.<P>Kit will be 2 replacement lower sail panels, 2 lower door skins(from the moulding down), 2 scoops for mounting behind the sail panels with round outlets to route the air to location/s of your choice (bolt onto the rear) and 2 black metal mesh grills for mounting inside the vents (optional, mount them or chuck them, still part of the kit Also considering offering them in chrome as an optional extra). I have scrapped the 2 small pieces on the front fenders for the sake of a small bulge 2" long that would need moulding in. Scoops door section will blend out at the front edge of the new lower door skins.<P>Still working on some detail drawings of both sides of the panels to show the scoops behind the panels. Thought I would have them done by now but I got stuck surfing the forum tonight.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>||||reg||1
