Z||000019||mrfixit58||08-01-2001||10:10 AM||||Aus,<P>I was looking at your Stage 2 rendering again and was wondering about something you said: Paraphrased, you said the little piece above the rocker panel behind the front fender was eliminated. <P>For those with GTs or SEs, are we going to have to remove the small factory molding that is in this location (the small piece at the bottom of the fender above the aero rocker molding) to make the Stage 2 scoop look right?<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000020||AusFiero||08-02-2001||11:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>Aus,<P>For those with GTs or SEs, are we going to have to remove the small factory molding that is in this location (the small piece at the bottom of the fender above the aero rocker molding) to make the Stage 2 scoop look right?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>No in hindsight I have to make a piece to go there. Otherwise it gunna look pretty silly isn't it. Forgot the guard wraps back under without it. To used to looking at my GT only. looking at a basic coupe would have reminded me of that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also I will have some exact pricing up tomorrow. I had to bail on having a USA distributor after my accountant informed me of the Taxmans ramifications. Seems exporting business to business puts me under a different tax classification that will kill all sorts of current tax advantages in exporting and will also kill me at income tax time. Which in turn would have added huge extra expenses to the bodykits and parts. I would have liked to do it that way and apoligised to the USA dealer. But thems the breaks I suppose. You just can't mess with the taxman when he is such a bloody strange beast to work out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>||||reg||1
